                "reply_count": 9,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Earlier today, I held a press conference with Public Health Solutions \u2014 the largest WIC provider in New York \u2014 to sound the alarm on the looming lapse in WIC funding amid the government shutdown.\n\nWIC serves 40% of America\u2019s infants and stands as one of our nation\u2019s most essential anti-hunger programs. If this funding is allowed to lapse, mothers and children across the country will be left struggling to afford basic nutrition.\n\nCongress must act now to reopen the government and fully fund WIC before lasting harm is done to families who can least afford it.",
                "text_lang": "en",
